    "Notes Updated": "5/2/2025",
    "Scouting Notes": "Starter\n Velo jump! Up from 90 93 to sitting 92 95 and touching 97 this year\n Appears to have a 4 seam that rides, believe the two seam I was seeing is no longer\n Cutter in the low 90's is solid\n Slider is pretty sharp and has 1 to 7 movement in the 83 86 range, not a sweeper.\n Changeup looks solid, but the velo separation is only about 6 7 MPH\n Think he's an arm the org is higher on than outside sources would be",
    "Notes Updated 2": "7/20/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Starter\n Unable to get a velo read on Cornielle at the moment, but the fastball looks lively. Would guess around 89 92 on the velo. (closer to 90 93 once we had readings)\n Appears to have a 4 seam that rides and a 2 seam that rides but also runs a good amount.\n Slider is pretty sharp and has 1 to 7 movement, not a sweeper.\n Changeup looks good, has good depth, nice fade. \n The fact the Brewers have him fully stretched to 90+ pitch outings as a 20 year old makes me think they like the arm a lot.\n Need more looks and would like to know what the velo is, but I think this could be a pretty big time arm.",
